dt-bindings: gpu: arm,mali-bifrost: require the RK3576 clock trio

The generic schema allows one to three clocks with any names. On RK3576
the GPU needs exactly three and the names are load-bearing: the core clock
is the one firmware scales, and the bus and gate clocks are what firmware
reaches its registers over. A node missing the gate builds and boots right
up until the first rate request, which then wedges the CPU, so a typo here
is worth catching at validation rather than at runtime.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-bifrost.yaml	2026-07-24 14:17:26.000000000 +0000
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-bifrost.yaml	2026-08-03 00:10:53.114985920 +0000
@@ -134,6 +134,23 @@
       properties:
         compatible:
           contains:
+            const: rockchip,rk3576-mali
+    then:
+      properties:
+        clocks:
+          minItems: 3
+          maxItems: 3
+        clock-names:
+          items:
+            - const: core
+            - const: bus
+            - const: gate
+      required:
+        - clock-names
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
             const: amlogic,meson-g12a-mali
     then:
       properties:
